{"claims":[{"claim_text":"In local platform hearings around the country and the world, Americans talked of the need for compassion, empathy, a commitment to values, and the importance of being united in order to take on the challenges and opportunities of the new century.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Americans expressed similar themes in town halls in Nevada, policy roundtables in Philadelphia, and online gatherings held by Democrats Abroad.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Barack Obama's message emphasizes that alongside Americans' famous individualism, there's a belief that Americans are connected to each other.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Americans could choose to focus on their own concerns and live their lives in a way that tries to keep their individual stories separate from the larger story of America, but that is not who they are.", "claim_types":["characterization"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"If there's a child on the south side of Chicago who can't read, that matters to Americans, even if it's not their child.", "claim_types":["characterization"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"If there's a senior citizen in Elko, Nevada who has to choose between medicine and the rent, that makes Americans' lives poorer, even if it's not their grandmother.", "claim_types":["characterization"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"It is only when Americans join together in something larger than themselves that they can write the next great chapter in America's story.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[1]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```
